SECTION 4 — PERMISSIONS (Request All Required)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

The app must request and handle all of these permissions properly.
Each permission is explained to the user with a friendly Luna-style
message before the system dialog appears.

Required permissions:

RECORD_AUDIO
  — for voice input and conversation

READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE / READ_MEDIA_IMAGES / READ_MEDIA_VIDEO
  — for Storage access to browse, read, and reference files

WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE (API < 29)
  — for saving exports and conversation backups

CAMERA
  — for flashlight control (camera flash LED)

FOREGROUND_SERVICE
  — for background monitoring when user enables it

POST_NOTIFICATIONS (API >= 33)
  — for task reminders and health check-ins

RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED
  — for restarting reminders after device reboot

VIBRATE
  — for haptic feedback on notifications

INTERNET
  — for AI API calls

ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE
  — for detecting connectivity before API calls

BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE
  — for Accessibility Service integration

USE_FULL_SCREEN_INTENT
  — for full-screen reminder notifications

REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES (optional)
  — only if APK install is a future feature; skip unless needed

Permission handling rules:
- Never request a permission without first showing Luna explaining why
- If denied, preserve alternative functionality where possible
- If permanently denied, explain how to open Android Settings
- Never silently fail on missing permissions
- Group permission requests logically, not all at once

