SECTION 7 — BACKGROUND MODE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Background mode allows Luna to work without the app being open.
This is controlled by a toggle in Settings named:
"Background Mode — Luna সবসময় তোমার সাথে"

When Background Mode is OFF:
- Luna only works when the app is open
- No foreground service running
- No background monitoring
- Scheduled reminders from Task Manager still fire via WorkManager
  (this does not require background mode — reminders work always)

When Background Mode is ON:
- A persistent ForegroundService runs with a small notification
  ("Luna is with you ✨")
- Notification has a "Tap to open" and "Turn off" action
- Wake phrase detection is active (using SpeechRecognizer in background)
- When wake phrase is heard, Luna sends a notification or pops a
  floating chat bubble (use BubbleMetadata API on API >= 29)
- Health check-in reminders are more frequent
- Notification reminders from Task Manager still fire normally

Foreground service behavior:
- Uses a low-priority persistent notification (not intrusive)
- Does not drain battery excessively — wake phrase check uses
  low-power audio trigger, not continuous full recording
- Automatically stops if battery falls below 15% (configurable)
- User can stop it at any time from the notification
- Restarts on boot if Background Mode was ON when device shut down
  (uses RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED)

Battery optimization:
- Register for battery optimization exemption with explanation
- Explain why it is needed: "যাতে আমি ঘুমিয়ে না পড়ি তোমার ডাকে 🥺"
- Do not force the user to grant it; app works without it but may
  behave less reliably in background

